This patch is needed because the Solaris wrapper drives Chromium Rust helper
rules with a stable standalone toolchain instead of the Chromium bundled
nightly oriented environment.

What it does:
- filters Solaris unsupported linker flags before forwarding link args to rustc
- strips Chromium only -Z flags from rsp content
- enables RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 in the wrapper environment
- exits immediately on rustc failure
- synthesizes a minimal depfile when Solaris rustc does not emit one

Why it is needed:
- without it, V8 Rust helper crates fail on unsupported linker flags, nightly
  only flags, or missing depfiles on Solaris
